		<script type="application/ld+json" id="schema-global">{
  "@context": "http://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "WebSite",
      "@id": "https://www.hsbc.com/#/schema/website",
      "name": "HSBC Group corporate website | HSBC Holdings plc",
      "inLanguage": "en-GB",
      "description": "HSBC, one of the largest banking and financial services institutions in the world, serves millions of customers through its four global businesses.",
      "url": "https://www.hsbc.com"
    },
    {
      "@type": "VideoObject",
      "@id": "https://www.hsbc.com/#/schema/video/e3a91e8c-9218-4955-b018-5b11d3669229",
      "name": "‘Another quarter of positive performance’",
      "thumbnailUrl": "https://www.hsbc.com/-/files/hsbc/investors/hsbc-results/2026/3q/images/261027-pam-video-3q26-768x576.jpg?sc_lang=en-gb",
      "transcript": "<h2>3Q Results 2026\n</h2>\n<p><strong>Duration:</strong> <br>\n00:04:22\n</p>\n<p><strong>Speaker names:</strong> <br>\nPam Kaur, Group Chief Financial Officer, HSBC\n</p>\n<p><strong>[Text on screen]</strong><br>\n3Q Results 2026\n</p>\n<p>Pam Kaur<br>\nGroup Chief Financial Officer<br>\nHSBC\n</p>\n<p><strong>[Pam]</strong><br>\nOur third quarter results show the progress we are making, the performance we are delivering, and the potential we are building for the future.\n</p>\n<p>Revenue grew five percent to $18.7 dollars.\n</p>\n<p><strong>[Text on screen]</strong><br>\nStrong performance in third quarter<br>\nRevenues grew 5% to $18.7bn\n</p>\n<p><strong>[Pam]</strong><br>\nThis was broad-based across our four businesses and income lines.\n</p>\n<p><strong>[Text on screen]</strong><br>\nStrong performance in third quarter<br>\nProfit Before Tax $10.0bn [excluding notable items]<br>\nUp 10% year-on-year\n</p>\n<p><strong>[Pam]</strong><br>\nWe delivered strong profit before tax growth, up ten percent to $10 billion dollars.\n</p>\n<p><strong>[Text on screen]</strong><br>\nStrong performance in third quarter<br>\nAnnualised RoTE 18.8% year-to-date [excluding notable items]\n</p>\n<p><strong>[Pam]</strong><br>\nAnnualised return on tangible equity was 18.8 percent year to date, 1.1 percent higher than last year.\n</p>\n<p><strong>[Text on screen]</strong><br>\nFour high-returning businesses<br>\nAnnualised RoTE in excess of 17% [excluding notable items]\n</p>\n<p><strong>[Pam]</strong><br>\nAll four of our businesses grew deposits, with each delivering annualised return on tangible equity in excess of 17 percent, excluding notable items.\n</p>\n<p>The strength of our franchise has been demonstrated over the last twelve months, and again in this quarter.\n</p>\n<p><strong>[Text on screen]</strong><br>\nThe world&rsquo;s wholesale transaction bank<br>\nFee and other income grew by 11%<br>\nYear-on-year\n</p>\n<p><strong>[Pam]</strong><br>\nIn wholesale transaction banking, we grew fee and other income 11 percent year on year as clients continued to turn to us to help them navigate market complexity.\n</p>\n<p>Our balance sheet and franchise strength are particularly valuable in times like these.\n</p>\n<p><strong>[Text on screen]</strong><br>\nAsia&rsquo;s #1 Wealth Manager<br>\nNet new money in Asia $38bn [excluding notable items]\n</p>\n<p><strong>[Pam]</strong><br>\nIn wealth, net new money of $38 billion dollars in Asia this quarter brings our total year to date flows to more than $100 billion dollars, demonstrating why we are Asia's number one wealth manager.\n</p>\n<p>We also have a strong and growing deposit franchise.\n</p>\n<p>Deposits increased by a $105 billion this quarter, including held-for-sale balances.\n</p>\n<p>We are pleased to be the largest international participant in the Reserve Bank of India's Foreign Currency Non-Resident Bank deposit scheme, the second largest bank overall.\n</p>\n<p>And in Hong Kong, we saw another strong performance with $21 billion dollars of deposit growth.\n</p>\n<p>Here we are benefiting from being full owners of the two iconic banks, from the growth of Hong Kong and our continued investment.\n</p>\n<p>On the lending side, the strength of the housing market in Hong Kong is translating into mortgage growth, where we have a competitive range of fixed and floating products.\n</p>\n<p>In the UK, we are particularly pleased with the 13% commercial lending growth year on year.\n</p>\n<p>This reflects our leading position with the UK companies, which provides us with great opportunities.\n</p>\n<p>This broad-based performance shows why we are confident in meeting the targets we set out at the full year.\n</p>\n<p><strong>[Text on screen]</strong><br>\nTargets reiterated <br>\nRevenue rising to 5% <br>\nYear-on-year growth by 2028\n</p>\n<p>Return on Tangible Equity 17%\nOr better [excluding notable items]\n</p>\n<p>Dividends 50%\nOf EPS [excluding material notable items and related impacts]\n</p>\n<p><strong>[Pam]</strong><br>\nAnd we are reallocating costs from non-strategic or low-returning businesses towards growth opportunities while upgrading our operating model.\n</p>\n<p>Thereby creating further potential which we have yet to realise.\n</p>\n<p>This quarter's performance reflects the extraordinary dedication of our people, their commitment to our customers and clients, and their skills and expertise, especially during complex times.\n</p>\n<p>This gives me great pride.\n</p>\n<p>I am particularly proud of what we are achieving together.\n</p>\n<p><strong>[Text on screen]</strong><br>\nHSBC | Opening up a world of opportunity\n</p>\n<br>\n<p>&copy; HSBC Group 2026</p>",
      "uploadDate": "2026-10-27T11:41:12"
    }
  ]
}</script>

